---
import { ACTION_QUERY_PARAMS } from 'astro:actions';
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="It All Starts With Writing | Justin Ho"
  description="A personal reflection on writing, clarity, and how ideas take shape before they become reality."
>

<article class="journal-post">
    <a href="/journal" class="back-link">← Back to Journal</a>
  <header class="journal-header">
    <p class="journal-label">Journal</p>
    <h1>It All Starts With Writing</h1>
    <p class="journal-meta">13 June 2026 · Writing</p>
    <p class="journal-intro">
      A reflection on writing, clarity, and how ideas begin to take shape.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="journal-content">
    <p>Many years ago, a lecturer said something that stayed with me.</p>

    <p>“It all starts with writing.”</p>

    <p>At the time, I thought he was talking about filmmaking.</p>

    <p>Today, I think he was talking about life.</p>

    <p>Looking back, I’ve noticed something strange.</p>

    <p>
      Many of the things that now occupy my life existed as words long before
      they became reality.
    </p>

    <p>LifeGate was writing before it was a business.</p>

    <p>My website was writing before it was a website.</p>

    <p>The apps I’m building were writing before they became software.</p>

    <p>Even this article started as a few sentences typed into a chat.</p>

    <p>
      When people talk about manifestation, they often imagine thoughts
      magically becoming reality.
    </p>

    <p>My experience has been much less mysterious.</p>

    <p>The things that changed my life were not the things I thought about.</p>

    <p>They were the things I wrote down.</p>

    <p>Writing forces an idea to leave the imagination.</p>

    <p>
      It gives shape to something that previously existed only as a feeling.
    </p>

    <p>
      The moment an idea is written, it becomes something you can question,
      refine, improve and eventually act upon.
    </p>

    <p>Perhaps that’s why writing feels so powerful.</p>

    <p>Not because it manifests reality.</p>

    <p>But because it creates clarity.</p>

    <p>And clarity has a way of becoming action.</p>

    <p>
      Looking back, I realise that many of the things I am building today began
      in exactly the same place.
    </p>

    <p>A blank page.</p>

    <p>A passing thought.</p>

    <p>A few words written down before they disappeared.</p>

    <p>Maybe that’s why I still write.</p>

    <p>
      Because every meaningful project in my life seems to start the same way.
    </p>

    <p>With words.</p>
  </section>
</article>
</MainLayout>

